{{define "description"}}What the City of Livermore budgets to pay on each debt, and the principal and interest its debt agreements schedule through 2055, every figure linked to the budget page it was read from.{{end -}}
{{template "head" .}}

<header class="page-head">
  <div>
    <h1>{{.Title}}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{.Lede}}</p>
  </div>
</header>

{{- define "debt-cell"}}
{{- if .Missing}}<td class="num debt-unprinted"><span title="The page prints no figure here">not printed</span></td>
{{- else}}<td class="num"><a href="{{.Href}}" title="{{if .Dash}}Printed as a dash, which is zero; {{end}}read on page {{.Page}}">{{.Value}}</a></td>
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
<main>

<details class="how-to-read" open>
<summary>About these figures</summary>
<p class="lede">
  {{.Facts}} figures, every one printed on Budget Book pages 80 and 81 and linked to the
  page it was read from. A dash is the city's printed zero. "Not printed" is a cell the
  page leaves blank, which is not a zero.
</p>
</details>

<h2 id="by-issue">Debt service budget, by issue</h2>
<p class="subtle">
  What the budget sets aside to pay on each debt: the FY 2024-25 revised budget and the two
  adopted years.
</p>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table class="series-table debt-table">
  <caption>Debt service by issue, principal and interest</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col" rowspan="2">Issue</th>
      {{- range .Columns}}
      <th scope="colgroup" colspan="2" class="num">{{.}}</th>
      {{- end}}
    </tr>
    <tr>
      {{- range .Columns}}
      <th scope="col" class="num">Principal</th><th scope="col" class="num">Interest</th>
      {{- end}}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  {{- $span := .HeadSpan}}
  {{- range .Activities}}
  <tbody>
    <tr class="block-head"><th scope="colgroup" colspan="{{$span}}">{{.Heading}}</th></tr>
    {{- range .Rows}}
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">{{.Label}}{{if .Payer}} <span class="subtle">· {{.Payer}}</span>{{end}}</th>
      {{- range .Cells}}{{template "debt-cell" .Principal}}{{template "debt-cell" .Interest}}{{end}}
    </tr>
    {{- end}}
  </tbody>
  {{- end}}
</table>
</div>

<h2 id="requirements">Debt service requirements through 2055</h2>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table class="series-table debt-table">
  <caption>Debt service requirements, principal and interest, by fund type</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col" rowspan="2">Year ending June 30</th>
      {{- range .FundTypes}}
      <th scope="colgroup" colspan="2" class="num">{{.}}</th>
      {{- end}}
    </tr>
    <tr>
      {{- range .FundTypes}}
      <th scope="col" class="num">Principal</th><th scope="col" class="num">Interest</th>
      {{- end}}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {{- range .Periods}}
    <tr{{if .Band}} class="debt-band"{{end}}>
      <th scope="row">{{.Label}}{{if .Band}} <span class="debt-band-note">{{.Years}} years in one figure</span>{{end}}</th>
      {{- range .Cells}}{{template "debt-cell" .Principal}}{{template "debt-cell" .Interest}}{{end}}
    </tr>
    {{- end}}
  </tbody>
  <tfoot>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Total, every row</th>
      {{- range .Totals}}
      <td class="num">{{.Principal.Value}}</td><td class="num">{{.Interest.Value}}</td>
      {{- end}}
    </tr>
  </tfoot>
</table>
</div>
<p class="subtle">
  Each total adds the figures above it, and this site checks it against the Total the page prints
  beneath the column.
</p>

{{- template "caveats-line" .CaveatsHere}}

</main>

{{template "footer" .}}

</body>
</html>
